    "description": "Pin every action to a commit SHA, so a repo that requires SHA pins can call the workflow\n\n## Why\n\n`jerridan/websites` requires SHA pins (`sha_pinning_required`). That rule also covers every action of a reusable workflow that the repo calls. The tag refs in `review.yml` and `action.yml` would stop the run there.\n\n## What\n\n- Pin `actions/checkout` (v4.4.0), `actions/upload-artifact` (v4.6.2) and `actions/setup-node` (v4.4.0) to commit SHAs in `action.yml`, `review.yml` and `ci.yml`.\n- Pin the action step of `review.yml` to `0f40cd3`, the first commit of this PR, where `action.yml` holds the pin.\n- Change the packaging tests to require full commit SHAs.\n- Update the release steps in the README, and tell a strict consumer to call the workflow at a SHA.\n\n## Merge\n\n**Merge with a merge commit, not a squash.** The action step points to `0f40cd3`. A squash drops that commit from `main`.\n\nThen move `v1` to the merge commit.\n\n🤖 Generated with [Claude Code](https://claude.com/claude-code)",
